      "source": "Magaliesbergkranse, a, Skeerpoort",
      "description": "Southern cliffs of the Magaliesberg, near Skeerpoort, South Africa. Even during this dry summer, water was seeping from the rock cracks, sustaining animals and vegetation. Numerous cremnophytes are visible, with their roots lodged in vertical rock crevices. The northward tilt in the ancient rock strata, a feature of the whole range, is very evident. These sedimentary strata are some 2.3 billion years old, and were tilted by igneous activity some 2.06 to 2.05 billion years ago.",
